  "summary": "Static tests verify correct/wrong PIN checking, per-hash random salts, length/numeric/repeated-digit validation, and stored iteration count used at verification. PinHasher uses PBKDF2-SHA256, random 16-byte salts, 32-byte hashes and fixed-time comparison; new/change PIN hashing validates length and repeated-digit strength, while HashWithoutValidation is explicitly for legacy backfill. The API is a financial authorization dependency, but the reviewed test/source path shows no new financial-integrity finding. Persistence-corrupted iterations/base64 could make Verify throw; stored-input hardening is not covered here and no reachable exploit was established. No tests executed.",
